# Connect your own domain

{% info title="SMTP-DOCS-TODO: Screenshot pending (blog-custom-domain)" %}
**SMTP-DOCS-TODO screenshot:blog-custom-domain.** Capture the Console screen that shows the MX and TXT records for a new email domain. Dark theme, 1460x822 viewport at 2x, screenshot mode on. Save as `/images/blog/announcing-function-email-triggers/custom-domain.avif`, then replace this block with the image.
{% /info %}

You can connect a domain that you own, such as `mail.example.com`. Email to any address at that domain executes your function. To verify the domain, add two DNS records at your registrar:

- An `MX` record that points the domain to the Appwrite mail server.
- A `TXT` record at `_appwrite.mail.example.com` with the verification token from the Console.

The email rule and the HTTP rule of a domain are separate. A domain such as `support.example.com` can serve a site and also send its email to a function.

